[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   Step 106 -- harmonic-order transfer, third-cohort axis recovery,
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   and cross-solution per-comet concordance.
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   Three remaining questions on the slip map are closed out here,
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   using only existing per-comet products (no new integrations).
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   T1  Third-cohort axis recovery.  The original convergence test
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   (step_036) let the CODE cohort recover its own axis by a free
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   sky scan; it landed 24 deg off the TNO axis.  The identical
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   scan is run on the one-apparition cohort (step 105 products):
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   a 10-deg grid of trial axes, Mann-Whitney in-cap vs out-cap
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   on the catalogue rotation d_of, best axis and the rank of the
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   pre-declared axis among all trial directions.
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   T2  Harmonic-order out-of-sample discrimination.  The bipolar
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   cos(2 theta) morphology was selected in-sample (step 089:
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   cos2 beats cos1 at p=0.010 vs 0.30), so the predictive
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   tests inherit a selection on the same data.  The five-fold
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   CV of step 102 is therefore rerun with alternative profile
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   families -- constant, cos(theta), cos(2theta), cos(3theta),
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   and a linear theta term -- under identical folds.  If
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   cos(2theta) retains the best held-out skill, the bipolar
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   form is confirmed predictively, not just descriptively.
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   T3  Amplitude transfer.  The lpc cohort's own free fit
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   dtau = a + b cos(2theta) returns b_lpc with a bootstrap
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   interval, compared against the 229-fitted b = +5.98 yr --
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   an amplitude consistency check that per-object rho cannot
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   deliver.
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   T4  Cross-solution per-comet concordance.  On the 23 members
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   shared between the lpc cohort and the training set, the
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   same bodies carry two different orbit solutions.  If the
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   anomaly is an object property, the per-comet discrepancies
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   should correlate across solutions; if it is a fit artefact,
[2026-09-20 12:20:28 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 106]   they should not.
